 "excerpt": "Calls for proposals, grants, tenders and expressions of interest relevant to organisations working in Bangladesh. Every listing shows the funder, size, deadline and status, and links to the original notice. Open now Opportunity Funder Size Deadline Status Medium-size grants for ecosystem-based adaptation Global EbA Fund (IUCN, UNEP; IKI funding) Up to USD 500,000 16 Nov [...]",
 "content": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.588), 20px);line-height:1.5\">Calls for proposals, grants, tenders and expressions of interest relevant to organisations working in Bangladesh. Every listing shows the funder, size, deadline and status, and links to the original notice.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Open now</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"color:#5c5c5c;font-size:14px\">Last checked: 24 November 2026.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Opportunity</th><th>Funder</th><th>Size</th><th>Deadline</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.ungm.org/Public/Notice/322127\">Evaluation and impact assessment for mental health programmes in Bangladesh (RFP-SEARO-Bangladesh-2026-013)</a><br><small>Tender for firms and organisations with evaluation and research capacity. Eligibility details are in the RFP documents on UNGM. Deadline 14:00 Dhaka time.</small></td><td>World Health Organization (WHO) Bangladesh</td><td>Not stated</td><td>25 Nov 2026</td><td><strong>CLOSING SOON</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.ungm.org/Public/Notice/322642\">Two External National Collaborators for the EPZ Model Zone Initiative with BEPZA (rfx_14397_ROAP)</a><br><small>For individual national consultants. Published on UNGM on 16 November. Deadline 11:30, listed as GMT+1.</small></td><td>International Labour Organization (ILO) Bangladesh</td><td>Not stated</td><td>26 Nov 2026</td><td><strong>CLOSING SOON</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.apn-gcr.org/news/2026-call-for-proposals-under-the-crrp-and-capable-programmes/\">2026 call for proposals: Collaborative Regional Research (CRRP) and Scientific Capacity Development (CAPaBLE)</a><br><small>For researchers and practitioners at institutions in APN member and approved countries, including Bangladesh. South Asia themes include climate resilience and loss and damage, nature-based solutions, and food, water and energy security. Summary proposals first, by 23:59 Japan time (20:59 Dhaka); full proposals by invitation.</small></td><td>Asia-Pacific Network for Global Change Research (APN)</td><td>Not stated</td><td>30 Nov 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.yves-rocher-fondation.org/en/how-to-apply-for-the-international-award/\">Terre de Femmes International Award 2027: \"Trees in the City\"</a><br><small>Open worldwide. Projects led by a woman or group of women, run through a non-profit at least one year old. The foundation's page is headed 2027 but gives a 2026 deadline, so confirm with the funder.</small></td><td>Yves Rocher Foundation</td><td>EUR 10,000 each (2 winners)</td><td>30 Nov 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.ungm.org/Public/Notice/320246\">Strengthening WASH and energy resilience for children in climate-stressed areas of Bangladesh (LRPS-2026-9206944)</a><br><small>For construction firms or agencies registered in Bangladesh with at least seven years of WASH and WASH in Schools experience. About 18 months of work in 20 schools in Ashulia. Deadline 11:00 Dhaka time.</small></td><td>UNICEF Bangladesh</td><td>Not stated</td><td>30 Nov 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://asiafoundation.org/the-asia-foundation-opens-applications-for-2027-development-fellows/\">Asia Foundation Development Fellows 2027</a><br><small>For individuals, not organisations: Bangladeshi citizens or residents under 40 on 1 January 2027, fluent in English. Fellows get a professional development award of up to $2,500.</small></td><td>The Asia Foundation</td><td>Up to $2,500 per fellow</td><td>1 Dec 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://d-prize.org/\">D-Prize: funding to start organisations that distribute proven poverty solutions</a><br><small>For new organisations, usually under 18 months old and under $30,000 raised. No country restrictions listed. The regular deadline passed on 15 November; the extension deadline needs registration and closes at midnight Pacific Time.</small></td><td>D-Prize</td><td>Up to $20,000</td><td>6 Dec 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.adb.org/news/events/community-resilience-partnership-program-partnership-forum-2027-call-solutions\">Community Resilience Partnership Program Forum 2027: call for solutions</a><br><small>One-page proposals on locally led climate and health adaptation from practitioners in South Asia, Southeast Asia and the Pacific; women especially encouraged. ADB pays travel for selected presenters to the forum in Bangkok on 23 and 24 February 2027. Not a project grant.</small></td><td>Asian Development Bank (ADB)</td><td>Travel support</td><td>15 Dec 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://innovation.wfp.org/wfp-innovation-challenge\">WFP Innovation Challenge</a><br><small>Equity-free funding for organisations with an innovation at least at minimum viable product stage. Applications are accepted on a rolling basis.</small></td><td>World Food Programme (WFP) Innovation Accelerator</td><td>Not stated</td><td>Rolling</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Recently closed</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Opportunity</th><th>Funder</th><th>Deadline</th><th>Status</th></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.ungm.org/Public/Notice/320757\">Post-campaign coverage survey for the 2026 measles-rubella vaccination campaign (LRPS-2026-9206993)</a></td><td>UNICEF Bangladesh</td><td>22 Nov 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.ungm.org/Public/Notice/320726\">Child journalist training (LRPS-2026-9206994)</a></td><td>UNICEF Bangladesh</td><td>22 Nov 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.ungm.org/Public/Notice/320781\">Enhancement of the VaxEPI immunisation platform: feature changes, microservice architecture and post-launch support (LRPS-2026-9206995)</a></td><td>UNICEF Bangladesh</td><td>23 Nov 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"/2026/10/29/open-call-global-eba-fund-medium-size-grants-of-up-to-500000-for-ecosystem-based-adaptation/\">Medium-size grants for ecosystem-based adaptation</a></td><td>Global EbA Fund (IUCN, UNEP; IKI funding)</td><td>16 Nov 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.undp.org/press-releases/innovators-wanted-undp-launches-usd-1-million-global-challenge-healthier-ocean\">Ocean Innovation Challenge, 5th call: marine pollution, coastal restoration and blue economy</a></td><td>UNDP, funded by Sida</td><td>15 Nov 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr><tr><td>Small-size grants for ecosystem-based adaptation</td><td>Global EbA Fund</td><td>26 Oct 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://asiapacific.unwomen.org/en/programme-implementation/2026/09/unw-ap-bgd-cfp-2026-003-addressing-the-medium-to-long-term-reintegration-needs-and-strengthening-social-protection-support-mechanisms-for-the-social-inclusion-of-bangladeshi-migrants\">Reintegration and social protection for Bangladeshi women migrants (CSO partner)</a></td><td>UN Women Bangladesh</td><td>15 Oct 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How we list opportunities</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>We link to the funder&#8217;s own notice wherever one exists.</li>\n\n\n<li>Status labels are OPEN, CLOSING SOON (seven days or less), UPCOMING and CLOSED. We never describe an expired call as open.</li>\n\n\n<li>Each listing shows the date we last checked it. Deadlines can change, so always confirm with the funder.</li>\n\n\n<li>Featured placement may be paid for in future. Paid listings will always be labelled and will never change a listing&#8217;s status or details.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Funding Tracker</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We are building a tracker of who funds what in Bangladesh: major donors, thematic priorities, humanitarian and development financing, climate finance and localisation. Read our first funding analysis on the <a href=\"/2026/10/29/rohingya-response-the-2026-appeal-is-a-quarter-smaller-and-still-underfunded/\">Rohingya response appeal</a> and the <a href=\"/2026/10/29/new-atlantic-council-brief-examines-bangladeshs-changing-aid-landscape/\">changing aid landscape</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"/submit/\">Submit a funding opportunity</a> · <a href=\"/category/funding/\">All funding coverage</a></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"color:#5c5c5c;font-size:14px\">Top image: the Sundarbans mangrove forest. Photo: Amdadphoto / <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mangrove_River_Maze.jpg\">Wikimedia Commons</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.</p>\n\n\n",
